  fishName: Tyrantworm
  description: The Tyrantworm is a huge, slow-moving ambush-predator. It's hunting
    tactics are simple- simply lie in wait with its lure hanging in front of its
    mouth. On Lantis, where most things use some form of bioluminescence to hunt,
    see, or attract a mate, the tyrantworm never has trouble attracting curious prey.\n\nChef's
    Notes:\n How huge! Unlike the Wale, this one only has quantity on its side. Its
    meat is... voluminous. It's certainly... expansive. What on earth am I going
    to do with all this...
